---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Commercial EPC Glasgow & Across Scotland"
  description="Commercial EPC assessments in Glasgow and across Scotland for landlords, agents and property owners. Clear reporting and reliable turnaround."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Commercial Energy Assessments</p>
      <h1 class="section-title">
        Commercial EPC Assessments in Glasgow and Across Scotland
      </h1>

      <p class="lead">
        Scottish Energy Services provides commercial Energy Performance
        Certificates for offices, retail units, industrial buildings, hospitality
        premises and other non-domestic properties throughout Glasgow and Scotland.
        We manage the assessment, calculation and certificate lodgement while
        keeping you informed throughout the process.
      </p>

      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/quote">
        Request a Commercial EPC Quote
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>When is a commercial EPC required?</h2>

      <p>
        A valid non-domestic EPC is generally required when a commercial building
        is constructed, sold or let to a new tenant. The energy performance rating
        must also be included when an applicable property is advertised for sale
        or rent.
      </p>

      <p>
        Some buildings are exempt, and larger non-domestic properties in Scotland
        may have additional requirements under Section 63. We can review your
        building and help establish which assessment is appropriate before work
        begins.
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href="/services/section-63-assessments">
          Learn about Section 63 assessments
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Who we work with</h2>

      <p>
        We support individual property owners, commercial landlords, letting
        agents, developers, solicitors, asset managers and organisations managing
        larger property portfolios.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Commercial landlords preparing a property for a new tenancy</li>
        <li>Owners selling or refinancing non-domestic premises</li>
        <li>Agents managing commercial sales and lettings</li>
        <li>Developers completing new-build or converted commercial space</li>
        <li>Businesses checking the energy performance of occupied premises</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What is included in the assessment?</h2>

      <p>
        Our commercial EPC service covers the information gathering, building
        assessment and technical work required to produce and lodge the
        certificate.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Initial review of the building and instruction requirements</li>
        <li>Site survey by a qualified non-domestic energy assessor</li>
        <li>Review of the building fabric, use, lighting and building services</li>
        <li>Energy modelling using the appropriate approved methodology</li>
        <li>Production and lodgement of the commercial EPC</li>
        <li>Recommendations showing potential energy-efficiency improvements</li>
        <li>Clear explanation of the result and any relevant next steps</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Our commercial EPC process</h2>

      <h3>1. Property and scope review</h3>
      <p>
        Send us the property address, building type, approximate floor area and
        reason for requiring the EPC. We will confirm the scope, fee and available
        appointment dates.
      </p>

      <h3>2. Site assessment</h3>
      <p>
        Our assessor visits the property to record the information required for
        the energy model. Floor plans, details of heating and cooling systems and
        any previous EPC can help make the process more efficient where available.
      </p>

      <h3>3. Calculation and lodgement</h3>
      <p>
        We complete the energy model, carry out the required checks and lodge the
        completed certificate on the Scottish EPC Register.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Commercial EPC coverage</h2>

      <p>
        We are based in Glasgow and complete commercial EPC assessments throughout
        Glasgow, Lanarkshire, Edinburgh, the Central Belt and wider Scotland. We
        can also coordinate work across multiple properties for landlords, agents
        and portfolio clients.
      </p>

      <p>
        For properties outside Scotland, contact us with the location and project
        details so we can confirm coverage and the applicable assessment
        requirements.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Commercial EPC FAQs</h2>

      <h3>How quickly can a commercial EPC be completed?</h3>
      <p>
        Most standard instructions are completed within 3–6 working days,
        depending on property access, building complexity and the information
        available. Urgent appointments may be possible where capacity allows.
      </p>

      <h3>What information should I provide?</h3>
      <p>
        Start with the property address, approximate floor area, current use and
        required completion date. Floor plans, building-services information and
        any previous EPC should also be provided when available.
      </p>

      <h3>Can you assess larger or more complex buildings?</h3>
      <p>
        Yes. We work with different types and sizes of non-domestic property. We
        will review the building before confirming which assessment method and
        evidence are required.
      </p>

      <h3>Does an EPC include improvement recommendations?</h3>
      <p>
        Yes. The assessment includes recommendations identifying measures that
        could improve the building’s energy performance. Their suitability will
        depend on the property, its systems and the intended use of the building.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Request a commercial EPC quote</h2>

      <p class="lead">
        Send us the property details and your required timescale. We will review
        the instruction and return a clear quotation with the next available
        appointment.
      </p>

      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/quote">
        Get a Commercial EPC Quote
      </a>

      <p>
        Alternatively, <a href="/contact">contact Scottish Energy Services</a>
        to discuss the property before requesting a quotation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>